# Read only by the test run, and committed on purpose.
#
# Vitest runs in Vite's "test" mode, and .env.test outranks .env.local — which is exactly what is
# needed here. Without this file the suite's behaviour depends on whether the person running it
# happens to have a proxy configured locally: `usingProxy()` flips, the app stops asking for the
# user's own API key, and a dozen tests about that path fail on one machine and pass on another.
#
# Tests that want the proxy set it themselves. The default is "no proxy configured", which is both
# the state a new contributor's machine is in and the state the published web app was in for
# months, so it is the one worth defaulting to.
VITE_SCAN_PROXY_URL=
VITE_APP_TOKEN=
